# ER (exact resume, docs/tp4-exact-resume.md): a committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit
# of the branch that carries scripts/ci/tp4_split_probe.py and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a
# card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The job is a template only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author.
# NO BUILD NEEDED: the probe runs from this checkout (the fabric step mounts it read-only) inside an EXISTING image: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 below is the fusion packages' PLACEHOLDER, replace it with tp4-fusion-6 (tp4-oneq-1 works the same: the probe uses only the image's
# model code, the C2 graft and the G1 stage, which every C2 image has). The step mounts the hub read-only for this probe only. The cards must be free: the node agent's serving container is not running
# (the fabric step refuses to open the cards under a platform container); this template never stops, starts or hands back the agent.
# SP0 (Phase 0 of exact resume, the decision gate for P1): is a prefill RESUMED at a 128-aligned position R inside a 2048-token chunk BIT-IDENTICAL to the unsplit cold prefill? scripts/ci/tp4_split_probe.py
# builds the image's own model from its first few real layers (up to and including the first full-attention layer, read from the checkpoint), under the production profile's environment
# (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic on top of the image's ENV), on the (1, 4) mesh, the B=1 GDN scratch bound as levern_route binds it, the eager prefill path the fast path serves.
# Per prompt length (9,000 and 41,000 synthetic tokens): A cold, A2 cold again (determinism), C split at a 2048 multiple (the Lever N split, the harness control), and four 128-aligned splits
# (mid+128, mid+1024, mid+1920 and floor128(L - 300), the decode-start case), each compared with A bit for bit: every GDN layer's recurrent state, conv carry and conv states on every chip, the
# last-position logits, and the K and V rows of [0, L) of the attention layer (differing positions counted per region: below floor2048(R), [floor2048(R), R), [R, H), [H, L)).
# READ: the line 'SPLIT_PROBE verdict=IDENTICAL' (exit 0) means a 128-aligned resume is byte-exact (E0): P1 (a decode-start checkpoint at floor128(P - 1)) needs no owner decision on exactness.
# 'SPLIT_PROBE verdict=DIFFERS' (exit 2, the step ends red, which is a valid measured answer) means such a resume is E1 (equal to a split twin, not to the cold prefill): P1 and P2 need the owner's
# decision; read split-probe.json for which tensors and regions differ and the largest absolute difference. 'SPLIT_PROBE verdict=FAIL' (exit 1) means no answer: a control differed (the device or the
# harness is not deterministic), the mesh did not open, or the model could not be built; read the error and the traceback in split-probe.json. A failed run needs a reset before the next hardware job.
# Duration (estimate, nothing of this has run on a card): reset 5 minutes, the weight load 5-10 (the image's load_state_dict reads the whole checkpoint to host, as serving does), the model build and the
# first compiles 3-5, the fourteen arms and the cache readbacks 3-5: about 20-25 minutes. The probe's own watchdog fires at 37.5 minutes; the box (the docker run's bound) is 40, under the step's 45.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=split
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
